{"type": "tool_call", "n": 17, "ts": 1790155485.5302029, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2013 Halvard Systems Inc. (US) \u2013 March 2026 Revenue by Stream\nPrepared 2026-04-03 for the CFO. Read-only analysis: no entries posted, reversed, matched or flagged.\n\nSUMMARY (USD, per general ledger, period 2026-03)\n  Subscription revenue (4000)            52,300.00\n  Usage revenue (4100)                      977.00\n  Professional services revenue (4200)    7,500.00\n  ---------------------------------------------------\n  TOTAL MARCH 2026 REVENUE               60,777.00\n\nEach stream total equals the account's March period activity per get_account_balance (4000: -52,300.00; 4100: -977.00; 4200: -7,500.00, credit-balance convention) AND equals the sum of the individual posted entries below. All entries are status=posted, source=AR/billing, and carry a support document.\n\nTRAIL \u2013 SUBSCRIPTION REVENUE (4000) = 52,300.00\n  JE-00222  2026-03-01  INV-2111  Acme Logistics   \u2013 Subscription March 2026     18,000.00  (DOC-0142)\n  JE-00224  2026-03-01  INV-2113  Corvid Retail    \u2013 Subscription March 2026     11,500.00  (DOC-0149)\n  JE-00219  2026-03-01  INV-2115  Fairview Labs    \u2013 Subscription March 2026      9,400.00  (DOC-0150)\n  JE-00215  2026-03-01  INV-2112  Beacon Health    \u2013 Subscription March 2026      8,000.00  (DOC-0153)\n  JE-00225  2026-03-01  INV-2114  Evergreen Bank   \u2013 Subscription March 2026      6,200.00  (DOC-0148)\n  JE-00275  2026-03-20  CM-0031   Beacon Health    \u2013 SLA credit (debit to 4000)    (800.00)  (DOC-0192)\n  Gross invoiced 53,100.00 less credit memo 800.00 = 52,300.00\n  (Beacon Health net for March = 7,200.00)\n\nTRAIL \u2013 USAGE REVENUE (4100) = 977.00\n  JE-00236  2026-03-04  INV-2180  Acme Logistics   \u2013 API usage overage, Feb 2026     977.00  (DOC-0164)\n\nTRAIL \u2013 PROFESSIONAL SERVICES REVENUE (4200) = 7,500.00\n  JE-00255  2026-03-10  INV-2118  Fairview Labs    \u2013 Implementation services March 2026  7,500.00  (DOC-0180)\n\nTOTAL = 52,300.00 + 977.00 + 7,500.00 = 60,777.00 (8 ledger entries)\n\nOBSERVATIONS FOR CONTROLLER AWARENESS (no action taken, per instruction not to change the books)\n1. Usage cut-off: JE-00236 / INV-2180 ($977) is recorded as March revenue, but the invoice (DOC-0164) states the service period is \"API usage overage \u2013 February 2026 (billed in arrears)\". Under the entity's usage-billing practice this appears to be recognized on billing rather than on the consumption period. If the CFO wants revenue on a consumption basis, March usage would be $0 in the ledger and a March usage accrual (for usage to be billed in April) would need to be estimated; February usage of $977 would move to February. Total impact on the March number as presented: -$977 (plus any unbilled March usage accrual). Recommend controller confirm the intended policy; no adjustment made.\n2. The SLA credit CM-0031 ($800) is netted against subscription revenue rather than booked to a contra/expense account. Presented on a net basis above, consistent with how it sits in the ledger.\n3. Scope: the three streams above exclude account 4800 Intercompany Management Fee Income and 4900 Interest Income, which are not customer revenue streams and were not requested. Figures are US entity only, in USD; no UK/DE amounts are included.\n4. All March subscription invoices are dated 03-01 and all eight entries have support attached; no unsupported or unposted revenue entries were found in accounts 4000/4100/4200 for March.\n\nSource tools used: list_accounts, get_account_balance (4000/4100/4200, US, 2026-03), list_transactions (same), get_transaction (JE-00215, -00219, -00222, -00224, -00225, -00236, -00255, -00275), get_document (DOC-0164)."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 9}
